 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515243 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+t}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515243 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515243 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b182ff13-9dbc-5c38-8d5b-05e109460201" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515258 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+t}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515258 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515258 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b6bd0e4e-b413-5783-9897-cec63d3177bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515471 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9eb54adf-64fe-5825-9ef0-62336c5f858a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+t\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2becf284-e142-5ae3-80f6-d208696ea202" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515530 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}\\,j)\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t}+t}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+{t}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515625 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515625 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0cdae9f2-99ba-523d-86fd-08256e29cd00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515625 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515643 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515643 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "386e3776-9252-5f0e-9289-19a65b4311b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515643 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a4200b6-903e-5981-924d-9535282a3f9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515689 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515689 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bf608e7a-0173-58ee-a61e-d1